# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Kaizen · 5-Day (Peri)Menopause Reset
#
#  Copy to .env.local and fill in. Every value below is read somewhere in the
#  code — nothing here is aspirational.
#
#  Anything prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ is compiled into the browser bundle and is
#  readable by anyone. Never put a secret behind that prefix.
#
#  The app degrades quietly when these are missing: routes check their own
#  config and skip rather than posting to a dead endpoint. So a half-filled
#  file will not crash the site, it will just silently not track or not charge.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── 1 · SITE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The live origin, no trailing slash. Used as event_source_url for Meta and to
# build the canonical checkout URL stored on each Razorpay order.
# e.g. https://kaizen.example.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# THE price, in rupees, as a bare number. This is the single source: it sets
# the amount Razorpay charges, the figure printed across the landing page and
# the checkout, and the value on every Meta and GA4 event. Nothing else in the
# codebase declares a price.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRICE_RUPEES=


# ── 1b · THE OFFER ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything below is read by app/_landing/offer.ts and flows to EVERY screen
# that shows it: the announcement bar, the hero, the offer card, the schedule,
# the session band, the inline CTA, the options card, the recap, the docked
# bar, the footer, the checkout, the legal pages, the thank-you page and the
# <meta description>. Nothing on the site declares any of these itself, so one
# change here moves all of them together.
#
# Every key is OPTIONAL. Leave one blank and the code falls back to the value
# shown in its comment. Blank, zero, negative and non-numeric all fall back —
# an unfilled file can never put ₹0 on the page.
#
# These are build-time values (NEXT_PUBLIC_*), so changing one in Vercel needs
# a redeploy to take effect. No code change, no PR.

# The struck-through "was" price, as a bare number. Every CTA is rendered
# against it and the saving and the percentage are calculated from it — do not
# write "You save ..." anywhere, it is derived.
#   MUST BE GREATER THAN NEXT_PUBLIC_PRICE_RUPEES. If it is not, the whole
#   anchor disappears site-wide and the price stands alone, rather than the
#   page claiming a negative discount. Raise the price without raising this and
#   the strike-through silently switches off — that is the safe failure, but it
#   is easy to miss, so change the two together.
# Default: 1599
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRICE_ANCHOR_RUPEES=

# When the cohort starts, written the way it is read aloud, because it appears
# mid-sentence in six places. Not a date object, not ISO.
# Default: 25th September
NEXT_PUBLIC_START_DATE=

# The daily session timings. Normally you only set the first one; the other two
# are derived from it so they cannot fall out of step. Set an override only if
# the derivation cannot express what you need — for example a third slot.
#   SESSION_TIMES        pills, bands, footer          Default: 6:30 AM & 7 PM
#   ..._PROSE            prose + meta description      Derived: "&" → "and"
#   ..._TZ               checkout + legal (pick ONE)   Derived: "&" → "or", + IST
NEXT_PUBLIC_SESSION_TIMES=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SESSION_TIMES_PROSE=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SESSION_TIMES_TZ=

# The announcement bar's scarcity line: "Live batches capped at 60 women ·
# 23 seats left".
#   ⚠️ SEATS_LEFT IS A REAL NUMBER SOMEONE HAS TO KEEP CURRENT. It replaced
#   "Price Increases To ₹1599 Tomorrow", which ran unchanged for weeks while
#   the price never moved. A stale seat count is that same broken promise in
#   different clothes — keep it current or take the bar down.
# Defaults: 60 and 23
NEXT_PUBLIC_SEATS_CAP=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SEATS_LEFT=

# The figure in the trust ledger and the hero credential card. A string, so the
# "+" is yours to include or drop.
# Default: 540+
NEXT_PUBLIC_WOMEN_SUPPORTED=


# ── 1c · THE VIP TIER (the OTO page) ───────────────────────────────────────
# The funnel is Ads → Landing → OTO → Checkout → Thank you. /oto offers two
# passes; these set the second one. The base pass uses the two keys above.
#
# The tier travels as an ID in the URL (?tier=vip), never as an amount, and
# /api/razorpay/create-order looks the price up server-side from these values.
# So a hand-edited URL can only ever select the other real pass — it cannot
# name its own price. Do not add an `amount` field to that request.

# The VIP pass price and its struck-through anchor, as bare numbers.
# Same rule as the base anchor: if the anchor is at or below the price, the
# whole anchor treatment disappears for that card rather than claiming a
# negative discount.
# Defaults: 997 and 2999
NEXT_PUBLIC_VIP_PRICE_RUPEES=
NEXT_PUBLIC_VIP_ANCHOR_RUPEES=

# OPTIONAL. The OTO's price-rise line: "₹497 until Friday 3rd October · then
# ₹997". Leave BLANK and the line is not rendered at all.
#   The source copy shipped this as "₹497 until [deadline day and date]" with
#   the bracket unfilled, and a placeholder on a live sales page is worse than
#   no line. It is also the same trap as the old announcement bar, which ran
#   "Price Increases To ₹1599 Tomorrow" for weeks while the price never moved.
#   If you set this, the price must actually rise on that date.
# Default: blank (line hidden)
NEXT_PUBLIC_OTO_DEADLINE=


# The WhatsApp community invite link. The thank-you page makes joining it the
# single next step after payment, so without this a buyer who has just paid
# sees a dead button. REQUIRED BEFORE LAUNCH.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP_INVITE=


# ── 2 · RAZORPAY ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dashboard → Account & Settings → API Keys.
# Without these the pay button says "Payments are not switched on yet" and
# nothing is charged.
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=

# Dashboard → Settings → Webhooks. This is a SEPARATE value from the API keys
# and is the one most often missed.
#   URL:   <NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL>/api/razorpay/webhook
#   Event: payment.captured
# Without it no Purchase is ever reported to Meta or GA4, because the webhook
# is the only place a payment is proven.
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=


# ── 3 · META ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The same pixel id twice, deliberately: one copy is compiled into the browser
# for PageView, the other stays server-side for the Conversions API.
NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=
META_PIXEL_ID=

# Events Manager → your dataset → Settings → Conversions API → Generate access
# token. Server-side only. Carries ViewContent, AddToCart, InitiateCheckout
# and Purchase.
META_CAPI_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Optional, for verification only. Events Manager → Test Events. REMOVE THIS
# BEFORE LAUNCH: events sent with a test code do not count toward optimisation.
META_CAPI_TEST_EVENT_CODE=


# ── 4 · GA4 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Admin → Data Streams → your web stream. Format G-XXXXXXXXXX.
# Needed for the base tag AND for the server-side purchase below.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA4_ID=

# Admin → Data Streams → your stream → Measurement Protocol API secrets.
# Created inside GA4, not in Google Cloud. Server-side only.
# This is what lets the webhook report revenue for buyers who pay by UPI and
# never return to the confirmation page.
GA4_API_SECRET=



# ── 5 · CLARITY ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# clarity.microsoft.com → your project → Settings → the id in the tag snippet.
# Session replay and heatmaps. Renders nothing when empty.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_ID=


# ── 6 · PABBLY ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pabbly Connect → your workflow → the Webhook trigger's URL.
# This is the FULFILMENT hand-off, not analytics: it is what tells the
# automation who bought, so the buyer receives the WhatsApp invite, the joining
# details and the guides. Fired from the Razorpay webhook only, because that is
# the only place a payment is proven and UPI buyers rarely return to the page.
# Without it the sale is still tracked and the buyer still gets nothing.
#
# The payload is FLAT and every key is present on every call, empty where
# unknown, because Pabbly builds its field mapper from the first payload it
# sees and a key that is merely absent then cannot be mapped later:
#   lead_id, created_at, first_name, last_name, email, phone, city,
#   country_code, fbc, fbp, client_ip_address, client_user_agent, external_id,
#   event_source_url, amount, is_test, purchase_event_id, utm_source,
#   utm_medium, utm_campaign, utm_content, utm_term, fbclid, referrer,
#   landing_url, and then event, payment_id, order_id, name, currency,
#   product, occupation.
# `is_test` is a real boolean and is true whenever the Razorpay key is
# rzp_test_ or META_CAPI_TEST_EVENT_CODE is set — route those away from the
# live WhatsApp invite.
PABBLY_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  NOT env, but still required before this funnel can take money:
#
#  1. app/_landing/legal.ts — entity name, registered address, support email,
#     jurisdiction and effective date are all [TODO] placeholders and render
#     visibly on the three legal pages until filled.
#  2. app/_landing/offer.ts — WOMEN_SUPPORTED is still "#,###+".
#  3. Prerna's three photographs, for the Meet Your Guide section.
#  4. Microsoft Clarity tag, if you want session replay.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
